<report>
<line><title>Logrank and Wilcoxon tests</title></line>
<block name="outer">
<line></line>
<line><title><in>title</in><in>strata</in>:</title></line>
<block name="groups">
<line></line>
<line><u><subtotal>For group <in>grp</in></subtotal></u></line>
<line>Observed deaths = <in>obs</in></line>
<line>Extent of exposure to risk of death = <inu>ext</inu></line>
<line>Relative rate = <inu>rel</inu></line>
</block>
<line></line>
<line>test statistics:</line>
<line><in>rank</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>variance-covariance matrix:</line>
<block name="covar"><line><in>mat</in></line></block>
<line></line>
<line>Chi-square for equivalence of death rates = <inu>chi</inu>  <pval><in>p</in></pval></line>
<block name="trends"><line>Chi-square for trend = <inu>trend</inu> <pval> <inp>p_trend</inp></pval></line></block>
<block name="strata">
<line></line>
<line><title><in>test</in> for COMBINED STRATA</title><subtotal>:</subtotal></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Deaths</th><th>Extent of exposure to risk of death</th><th>Relative rate</th></tr>
<block name="stratum"><tr><td><in>grp</in></td><td><in>res</in></td><td><inu>sum</inu></td><td><inu>tot</inu></td></tr></block>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>overall chi-square = <inu>chi_strata</inu>  <pval><inp>p_strata</inp></pval></line>
<block name="strata_trend"><line>Chi-square for trend = <inu>strata_trend</inu><pval>  <inp>p_strata_trend</inp></pval></line></block>
</block>
<block name="hazards">
<line></line>
<line></line>
<line>Hazard Ratio  <ci>(approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval)</ci></line>
<block name="hazard"><line><in>vs</in> = <inu>haz</inu>  <ci>(<inu>from</inu> to <inu>to</inu>)</ci></line></block>
<block name="cml">
<line></line>
<line>Conditional maximum likelihood estimates:</line>
<line>Hazard Ratio = <inu>hr</inu></line>
<line><ci>Exact Fisher <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>llf</inu> to <inu>ulf</inu></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact Fisher one sided <inp>p1f</inp>, two sided <inp>p2f</inp></pval></line>
<line><ci>Exact mid-P <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>llm</inu> to <inu>ulm</inu></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact mid-P one sided <inp>p1m</inp>, two sided <inp>p2m</inp></pval></line>
</block>
</block>
</block>
</report>
